  {
   "id": "aJCMSrahAwAJ",
   "from": "Bob Carpenter",
   "author": "8aa9b8cc06fdc99c",
   "date": "2017-05-13T23:08:32Z",
   "subject": "Re: [stan-users] gamma(.., ..)^2 -> generalized_gamma(?, ?, ?)",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "First thing to do is test your gamma implementations before\r<br>trying to fit.\r<br>\r<br>It helps if you say how things failed.\r<br>\r<br>Rather than log(tgamma(x)), you want lgamma(x).\r<br>\r<br>It should look like this:\r<br>\r<br>  return log(c)\r<br>         + c * a * log(b)\r<br>         + (c * a - 1) * log(x)\r<br>         - (b * x)^c\r<br>         - lgamma(a);\r<br>\r<br>then either use the function exposer in RStan or test within the\r<br>Stan program to make sure you get the right values using some kind\r<br>of independent implementation.\r<br>\r<br>- Bob\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "\r<br>&gt; On May 12, 2017, at 8:43 PM, S &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">mangiol...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; Hello,\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; I have shape and rate parameters of a gamma distribution that seem to be related as some form of rate=shape^2\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; Now I want to observe if rate followes a generalized_gamma distribution. Howeve my dummy attempts for developing such function failed in test\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; I found the generalised gamma function in BUGS \r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; \r<br>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "&gt; these are the attempts\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; #1\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; set.seed(1)   # for reproducible example\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; s = 50\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; r = 3\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; x &lt;- rgamma(10000,shape=s,rate=r)\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; stan(\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; \tmodel_code=&quot;\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; \tfunctions{\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; \t\treal ggamma_lpdf(real x, real a, real b, real c) {\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; \t\treturn( (c*a * (log (c) + log(b)) ) + ((c*a - 1) * log (x) ) + (-(b*x)^c ) - log( tgamma(a) ));\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; \t\t}\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; \t}\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; \tdata {\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; \tint&lt;lower=1&gt; G;\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; \tvector[G] y; \r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; \t}\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; \tparameters { real&lt;lower=0&gt; h[3]; }\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; \tmodel { for(g in 1:G) y[g] ~ ggamma(h[1], h[2], h[3]); }\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; \t&quot;, \r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; \tdata = list(G=length(x), y=x)\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; )\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; #2\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; set.seed(1)   # for reproducible example\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; s = 50\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; r = 3\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; x &lt;- rgamma(10000,shape=s,rate=r)\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; stan(\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; \tmodel_code=&quot;\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; \tfunctions{\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; \t\treal ggamma_lpdf(real x, real a, real b, real c) {\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; \t\treturn(log(c*b^(c*a) * x^(c*a - 1) * exp(-(b*x)^c) / tgamma(a)));\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; \t\t}\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; \t}\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; \tdata {\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; \tint&lt;lower=1&gt; G;\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; \tvector[G] y; \r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; \t}\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; \tparameters { real&lt;lower=0&gt; h[3]; }\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; \tmodel { for(g in 1:G) y[g] ~ ggamma(h[1], h[2], h[3]); }\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; \t&quot;, \r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; \tdata = list(G=length(x), y=x)\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; )\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; Thanks\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; \r<br>"
    ],
    [
     1,
